#algorithm
#Odd numbers leave a remainder when divided by 2, while even numbers do not.
#Use this property to determine the parity of a number.
#If there's a remainder, the number is odd; if not, it's even.
#This is a simple and direct way to distinguish between even and odd values.class Solution:
# Function to check if a number is odd
#time complexity-O(1)
#space complexity-O(1)
    def isOdd(self, n):
        return n % 2 != 0  # Return True if the number is odd, else False
